# media/ is deliberately NOT ignored. These files are already served publicly by
# the site, so tracking them leaks nothing — and since the S3 bucket that used to
# hold them was deleted, git is now their offsite copy. A fresh clone (and every
# deploy, which is a git pull) gets working images with no extra step.

